2. nearby-sharing/android — Windows Nearby Sharing / MS-CDP reference
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Project   : nearby-sharing (android client)
   Homepage  : https://github.com/nearby-sharing/android
   License   : Apache License 2.0 (as published in the project's LICENSE file)

   Used as the reference for:
     - the Microsoft Co-Discovery Protocol (MS-CDP) discovery beacon broadcast
       as BLE manufacturer data under Microsoft company id 0x0006, with the
       fixed-layout `BLeBeacon` (`[scenario=1][deviceType][version<<5|flags]
       [deviceStatus][mac6][deviceName]`) — the exact layout implemented by
       `MsCdpHandler`;
     - the NearShare control-message set (StartTransfer / FetchDataRequest /
       FetchDataResponse / CompleteTransfer / CancelTransfer / handshake),
       its pull-based 100 KiB partition flow, and the CDP session binary
       framing.

   Apache License 2.0 text is available at:
     https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.txt
   (also published in the upstream repository's LICENSE file).

