3. NearDrop (via Bada) — Quick Share PIN / key-derivation semantics
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Project   : NearDrop (grishka/NearDrop) — referenced by Bada
   Homepage  : https://github.com/grishka/NearDrop
   License   : GPL v3 (as published in the upstream repository's LICENSE file)

   The 4-digit Quick Share confirmation PIN implemented in this module
   (`GsCrypto.pinFromBytes`) is the Chromium algorithm ported verbatim from
   NearDrop's `pinCodeFromAuthKey` (mod 9973, multiplier 31, signed bytes,
   `abs(hash)` formatted to 4 digits), as adopted by Bada's
   `PinDerivation.deriveFourDigitPin`. The PIN seed is derived with
   HKDF-SHA256 using Bada's "UKEY2 v1 auth" salt.

