Notes
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- This module is self-contained: it does not import the "entry"
  module. All byte/crypto/transport utilities are re-implemented inside this
  module so the GPL boundary stays clean.
- The application shell accesses this module exclusively through
  the facade exposed by `entry/src/main/ets/protocol/gs/` (GsFacade + factory
  + adapter). No other entry source file imports gs internals.
- Wire constants were verified against the upstream sources referenced above
  (cloned and read at build time): the CDP beacon layout/scenario/device-type
  values, the Microsoft company id 0x0006, and the Quick Share PIN algorithm.
  The NearShare transport-layer exchange in this module is a self-consistent
  simplified variant (length-prefixed JSON control frames); byte-exact
  interop with stock Windows Nearby requires porting the full CDP binary
  session protocol (ValueSet serialization, 100 KiB pull-based FetchData, CDP
  encryption), which is documented at the definition site in
  `NearShareProtocol.ets`. Likewise, the Quick Share data plane here uses the
  task-frozen PBKDF2 + AES-256-GCM suite rather than the real Quick Share
  HKDF + AES-256-CBC/HMAC-SHA256 SecureMessage suite; the PIN derivation
  follows the reference algorithm exactly.